          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the force of friction disappears in the world? How will the motion of objects be impacted?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.088,
            0.889,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "it moving? On a moving object, we have to continuously apply a force to counter the force of friction. Otherwise, the force of friction acting against the direction of motion brings the object to rest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.222,
            0.142,
            0.807,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you remember doing an activity in an earlier grade where you found that the force of friction depends upon the nature of the surfaces in contact? Let us carry out a similar activity here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.812,
            0.15,
            0.881,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 8",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Curiosity "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 5",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
